    {
      "id": "7qgtp4e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Vegetative / Asexual Propagation"
    },
    {
      "id": "tzl8ded",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Method</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cutting (Stem/Leaf/Root)</p>",
            "<p>A plant part placed in rooting medium to generate roots</p>",
            "<p>Rose, sugarcane, grapes, tapioca, chrysanthemum</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Grafting</p>",
            "<p>Joining scion (desired variety) onto rootstock</p>",
            "<p>Mango (stone/epicotyl graft), citrus (T-budding), apple</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Budding</p>",
            "<p>Single bud inserted on rootstock; T-budding is most common</p>",
            "<p>Rose, citrus, rubber, mango</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Layering</p>",
            "<p>Root a stem while still attached to parent plant</p>",
            "<p>Litchi (air/gooti layering), guava, jasmine</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Division</p>",
            "<p>Separating plants into parts with roots</p>",
            "<p>Banana (suckers), pineapple (crowns/slips), strawberry</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Tissue Culture (Micropropagation)</p>",
            "<p>In vitro propagation using meristem; disease-free plants</p>",
            "<p>Banana, potato, sugarcane, cardamom, orchid</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "230puda",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.5 Post-Harvest Technology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d131do0",
      "content": "Post-harvest technology encompasses all operations from harvest to final consumption, aimed at minimising losses and maintaining quality of horticultural produce."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Differentiate clearly between Sexual Propagation (seed-based, genetic diversity) and Vegetative/Asexual Propagation (clones, true-to-type).",
        "Key concepts under Post-Harvest Technology, particularly causes of post-harvest losses and storage methods, are frequently asked in competitive exams.",
        "Classification and major growing areas of India's prominent fruit and vegetable crops form essential objective test material."
      ],
      "id": "oftnl1l"
    },
    {
      "id": "apg3n57",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Post-Harvest Losses"
    },
    {
      "id": "xda3565",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "India's post-harvest losses estimated at 15–25% for fruits and vegetables",
        "Causes: improper harvesting, handling, packaging, storage, transport"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sn801t8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Storage Methods"
    },
    {
      "id": "enln2k6",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Method</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Temperature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Suitable For</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Features</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Room Temperature Storage</p>",
            "<p>Ambient</p>",
            "<p>Dry grains, spices, onion, garlic</p>",
            "<p>Ventilated godowns; limited shelf life</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Refrigerated Cold Storage</p>",
            "<p>0–5°C</p>",
            "<p>Most fruits and vegetables</p>",
            "<p>Extends shelf life 2–4x; prevents ripening</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Controlled Atmosphere (CA)</p>",
            "<p>Low O2 (2–5%), High CO2 (1–5%)</p>",
            "<p>Apple, pear, kiwi, avocado</p>",
            "<p>Longest shelf life; expensive; maintains texture/colour</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Modified Atmosphere (MAP)</p>",
            "<p>Modified gas mixture in packaging</p>",
            "<p>Fresh-cut produce, berries, salads</p>",
            "<p>Less precise than CA; more economical</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Evaporative Cool Chambers</p>",
            "<p>Reduces temp by 10–15°C above ambient</p>",
            "<p>Short-term storage of vegetables</p>",
            "<p>Zero-energy cool chamber for villages (NHB)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Wax Coating</p>",
            "<p>Ambient</p>",
            "<p>Citrus, apple, mango, cucumber</p>",
            "<p>Reduces transpiration; extends shelf life; improves appearance</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
